# Ruling 2025-11-17: the abilities care about what mana was spent to pay Deceit's TOTAL cost, not just the hybrid symbols. Bot1 pays with Mox Sapphire,
# four Mox Jets and Mox Ruby: one blue, four black and one red are spent in all, and only one blue could have gone into the hybrid. Black spent is four, so
# the {B}{B} ability happens (Bot2 discards the Lightning Bolt) and the {U}{U} one does not (one blue): Llanowar Elves stays. The harness cannot name which
# symbol each mana pays (the engine decides the split once the choice is not ambiguous), so the split of hybrid and generic is not forced here; what is
# proven is that every mana spent counts, the generic's black included, and the single blue never reaches two.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Deceit
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Forest x4
Forest x12

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#3.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#4.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Deceit.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Hand.Count = 5
